      "writtenOn": "2026-11-05T01:20:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for raising this. The U suffix is removed to avoid Clang-tidy’s redundant-cast diagnostic on ARM32, where size_t is already unsigned int. \nSince rules.size() is unsigned, the usual arithmetic conversions convert 1 to size_t before subtraction.\nThere is no unsigned-to-signed promotion or signed intermediate. The explicit cast to unsigned remains to preserve the narrowing on platforms where size_t is wider. \nAlso, the vector starts with one reserved entry and emplace_back occurs before the subtraction, so the index calculation doesn’t underflow.",
